"decision":"block","drop_reason":null,"evidence":["autodeploy.sh:228 `[ \"$TARGET\" = \"$DEPLOYED\" ] && { rm -f \"$DEFER_FILE\"; log \"up to date ($TARGET); no-op\"; exit 0; }`","autodeploy.sh:245 `prune_docker_caches() {` — defined 17 lines below the plan's call site","Plan step 2: helpers added 'near the existing helpers (autodeploy.sh:~150)'; step 3: 'Call reclaim_under_pressure on the no-op early-exit line (autodeploy.sh:228)'"],"finding":"prune_docker_caches() is defined at autodeploy.sh:245, AFTER the line-228 no-op exit where the plan calls reclaim_under_pressure (which invokes prune_docker_caches). Bash resolves function names at call time, so invoking prune_docker_caches at line 228 with its definition still at 245 would hit an undefined function; the plan places the new helpers at ~150 but does not require moving prune_docker_caches above the line-228 call site.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f156753e6dc9a51ce","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 3 / Scope (autodeploy.sh:228 call site vs prune_docker_caches at autodeploy.sh:245)","norm_id":"nfcae42d2867902e6","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","scenarios":["A quiescent no-op tick with disk >= 80%: line 228 calls reclaim_under_pressure -> prune_docker_caches, which is not yet defined at that point in source order -> command-not-found, no reclaim happens."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Relocate the prune_docker_caches() definition (and, for cohesion, record_backoff_failure if needed) above line 228, or define root_disk_pct()/reclaim_under_pressure() alongside prune_docker_caches after line 245 and confirm no other early-exit calls them earlier.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes